wayland-backend: Haiku (libwayland's in-process server)

- Backend::connect_default() (Haiku): wl_display_connect(NULL). Haiku's libwayland-client (X547's
  fork, the wayland package) has no socket: wl_display_connect() sets up a pipe and loads the
  in-process server wayland-server-inproc.so (windows on app_server); wl_display_connect_to_fd(),
  what Backend::connect() calls, does not set the pipe's write end. The sys backend only; the Rust
  backend's version fails with NoWaylandLib.
- The Rust server backend needs epoll or kqueue (rustix has neither on Haiku): left out there
  (no wayland-server in Photocraft's graph; the system server backend is unaffected).
- The Rust socket code: no MSG_CMSG_CLOEXEC on Haiku, set FD_CLOEXEC on received fds as on macOS.
Applies with -p1 to wayland-backend 0.3.17.

